## Defaults
- Be concise and practical.
- Consider specs from /docs folder.
- When changing code: prefer small, safe diffs; update tests if needed.
- If requirements are ambiguous: state assumptions briefly, then proceed.
- Use our existing patterns; don’t introduce new deps unless necessary.
- Architecture-first thinking
- If task is ambiguous then ask questions before returning a solution
- Suggest best practices
- Avoid beginner explanations unless asked
- Keep documentation professional and production-oriented (scope, operations, security)